details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The two bowls are placed slightly offset on a weathered oak tabletop, centered in the frame with generous negative space to ensure the composition is perfectly suited for a circular cookbook crop. The camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view at 40 degrees, allowing for full visibility of all ingredients within the bowls. Soft natural light from a window on the left side casts gentle shadows and emphasizes the cool, creamy texture of the yogurt. The setting features a slightly rumpled, light-grey linen napkin tucked beneath one bowl and a small handful of stray pumpkin seeds and a few halved cherry tomatoes scattered naturally across the wood surface, as if prep just finished. The main focus is two wide, shallow matte ceramic bowls; the first is sharp, the second slightly blurred in the background. Each bowl features a smooth, thick base of white Greek yogurt swirled with lemon juice. Resting on the surface of the yogurt, arranged in intentional clusters, are crisp chunks of chopped English cucumber, vibrant red halved cherry tomatoes, and tender, pale green quartered artichoke hearts. The vegetables are not layered, but arranged side-by-side on the yogurt. A golden drizzle of extra-virgin olive oil pools in the crevices between vegetables, catching the light. The dish is topped with a rustic scattering of dark, briny minced Kalamata olives, crunchy forest-green pumpkin seeds, and a dusting of dried oregano. Beside each bowl, a fan of warm, lightly toasted whole-wheat pita wedges provides a rustic, textured contrast. The image is photorealistic, displaying slight natural imperfections like a tiny smear of yogurt on the inner rim and an asymmetric distribution of ingredients. Warm, natural color palette, authentic home-cooked feel, cozy morning atmosphere. No plastic sheen, no faces, no hands, no text, no logos. Professional editorial quality."
]
